{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder"],"declarations":32,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.feCert_boundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.feCert_boundary","kind":"theorem","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L300-L314","doc":"**Boundary identity, proved (fraction form)**: the operator's\ninhomogeneous part is the certificate's boundary value,\n`rhs(q,x) = −Cert(q,x,1)` — the content is the cancellation of the\n`(1−x)(1−qx)` factors, hence the hypotheses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.feCert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.feCert","kind":"def","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L291-L298","doc":"The 4₁ qZeilberger certificate, factored form (poles at `y = x, qx`):\n`Cert(q,x,y) = −y(qx+1)(qx²−1)(q³x²−1)(1−x)(1−qx)/(q·x⁷·(y−x)(y−qx))`.\nComputed and verified corpus-side\n(`computations/aj_figure_eight_certificate.py`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.figureEightOperator_annihilates_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.figureEightOperator_annihilates_one","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L270-L289","doc":"**Concrete-color annihilation, proved for N = 1**: the transcribed\noperator annihilates the tower at its base color — machine-checked\n(the general-`N` statement is the literature theorem carried by the\nclass instance below; `N = 1..12` are verified symbolically in the\nwitness). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.figureEightOperator_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.figureEightOperator_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L226-L268","doc":"**Nontriviality, proved** (char 0): for every `q ≠ 0` the top\ncoefficient is nonzero somewhere — witness `m = −1/q²` generically,\n`m = −2/q²` when `q³ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.feUnit_nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.feUnit_nondegenerate","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L218-L224","doc":"The unit factor is not identically zero (witness `M = 2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.figureEightOperator_specializes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.figureEightOperator_specializes","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L204-L216","doc":"**Specialization, proved**: at `q = 1` under the meridian-squared\nconvention the homogeneous part of the explicit operator equals\n`feUnit M · A_{4₁}(L, M)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.feUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.feUnit","kind":"def","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L200-L202","doc":"The strong-AJ unit factor of the `q = 1` specialization:\n`(M⁶ − M⁴ − M² + 1)/M¹⁶ = (M²−1)²(M²+1)/M¹⁶`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.figureEightOperator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.figureEightOperator","kind":"def","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L194-L198","doc":"The explicit annihilator of the 4₁ tower, as a `QDifferenceOperator`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.feRhs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.feRhs","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L190-L192","doc":"Inhomogeneous part of the explicit 4₁ annihilator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.feCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.feCoeff","kind":"def","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L181-L188","doc":"Coefficient functions of the explicit 4₁ annihilator (`j, q, m`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.aPolyFigureEight_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.aPolyFigureEight_def","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L164-L169","doc":"Sanity: the classical A-polynomial reference is the stated explicit\npolynomial (definitional anchor for reviewers diffing against CCGLS). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.coloredJones41_qholonomic_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.coloredJones41_qholonomic_bar","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L154-L162","doc":"**Derived (conditional): q-holonomicity transports across the bar\ninvolution** — the tower is q-holonomic at `q⁻¹` with the SAME tower\nvalues as at `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.annihilates_bar_transport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.annihilates_bar_transport","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L139-L152","doc":"**Bar transport of annihilators (unconditional — uses the PROVED bar\nsymmetry of the tower).**  Any operator annihilating the figure-eight\ntower at `q⁻¹` annihilates the *same numerical tower* as at `q`: by\n`coloredJones41_bar_symmetric` the two towers coincide pointwise, so\nthe bar involution moves annihilators without changing the annihilated\nobject.  This is the operator-level face of the amphichirality of\n`4₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.coloredJones41_qholonomic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.coloredJones41_qholonomic","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L131-L137","doc":"**Derived (conditional on the literature class): the figure-eight\ncolored Jones tower is q-holonomic at every `q ≠ 0`.**  Genuinely\nderived ∃-packaging of the class data (§3b-cond non-degenerate). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.StrongAJFigureEight.specializes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.StrongAJFigureEight.specializes","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L126-L126","doc":"**Specialization (the AJ content), meridian-squared convention**:\nat `q = 1`, with `m = M²` (the multiplication variable is the\nsquare of the meridian eigenvalue — the convention the corpus-side\nverification `aj_figure_eight_operator_construct_verify.py`\nidentified; the naive `m = M` map does not match), the homogeneous\npart equals `unit M · A_{4₁}(L, M)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.StrongAJFigureEight.unit_nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.StrongAJFigureEight.unit_nondegenerate","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L119-L119","doc":"The unit factor is not identically zero (the classical limit is not\nthe zero polynomial). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.StrongAJFigureEight.unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.StrongAJFigureEight.unit","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L116-L116","doc":"The strong-AJ unit factor relating the `q = 1` specialization to the\nclassical A-polynomial.  For the actual operator it is\n`(M²−1)²(M²+1)/M¹⁶` — an L-free factor in `M`, vanishing at the\ndegenerate meridians `M² = ±1`, so nondegeneracy (below) is the\nhonest condition, not pointwise nonvanishing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.StrongAJFigureEight.annihilates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.StrongAJFigureEight.annihilates","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L109-L109","doc":"Annihilates the (concrete, Lean-defined) colored Jones tower of `4₁`\nat every `q ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.StrongAJFigureEight.nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.StrongAJFigureEight.nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L106-L106","doc":"Non-trivial at every `q ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.StrongAJFigureEight.order_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.StrongAJFigureEight.order_eq","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L104-L104","doc":"The inhomogeneous presentation has order 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.StrongAJFigureEight.op","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.StrongAJFigureEight.op","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L102-L102","doc":"The annihilating operator (explicit in the literature). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.StrongAJFigureEight.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.StrongAJFigureEight.mk","kind":"ctor","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L100-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.StrongAJFigureEight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.StrongAJFigureEight","kind":"class","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L89-L129","doc":"**Strong AJ for the figure-eight (§3b class; literature theorem,\ninstance not fabricated).**  Carries, as content-bearing fields, the\nstatement proved in the literature (Ref: [nguyen-tran-2021]): an\nexplicit order-2 inhomogeneous q-difference operator annihilates the\ncolored Jones tower of `4₁` for every `q ≠ 0`, and its homogeneous part\nevaluated at `q = 1` equals the classical A-polynomial up to a nonzero\nunit factor `unit m`.  The sorry-free instance (explicit operator, all\nfields proved — general-`N` annihilation included) lives in\n`QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEightAnnihilation`; the empirical\nreconstruction is\n`computations/aj_figure_eight_operator_construct_verify.py`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.aPolyFigureEight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.aPolyFigureEight","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L83-L87","doc":"The classical A-polynomial of the figure-eight knot, as an explicit\ntwo-variable polynomial function (CCGLS tables):\n`A_{4₁}(L, M) = M⁴L² − (M⁸ − M⁶ − 2M⁴ − M² + 1)L + M⁴`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.IsQHolonomic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.IsQHolonomic","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L76-L81","doc":"A tower `J` is q-holonomic at `q` when some non-trivial q-difference\noperator annihilates it — the existence half of the AJ machinery\n(a THEOREM for all knots, Garoufalidis–Lê 2005; here stated as the\ntarget predicate). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.NontrivialAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.NontrivialAt","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L71-L74","doc":"Non-triviality of `op` at `q`: the top coefficient is not identically\nzero in `m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.Annihilates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.Annihilates","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L64-L69","doc":"`op` annihilates the tower `J` at deformation parameter `q`:\n`∑_j coeff_j(q, q^N) · J(N+j) = rhs(q, q^N)` for every color `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.QDifferenceOperator.rhs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.QDifferenceOperator.rhs","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L62-L62","doc":"Inhomogeneous right-hand side, as a function of `(q, m)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.QDifferenceOperator.coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.QDifferenceOperator.coeff","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L60-L60","doc":"Coefficient of the `j`-th shift, as a function of `(q, m)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.QDifferenceOperator.order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.QDifferenceOperator.order","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The order (L̂-degree) of the operator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.QDifferenceOperator.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.QDifferenceOperator.mk","kind":"ctor","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.QDifferenceOperator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.QDifferenceOperator","kind":"structure","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AJFigureEight.lean#L52-L62","doc":"An (inhomogeneous) q-difference operator acting on color towers:\n`order`, coefficient functions `coeff j q m` of the deformation\nparameter `q` and the multiplication variable `m = q^N`, and an\ninhomogeneous part `rhs q m` (`0` for a homogeneous operator). ","signatureChunk":0}]}